## Configure Flux

Similarly, the Flux brokers on the compute nodes need the same system instance
configuration, CURVE certificate and IMP configuration as the *head node*, as
well as the cryptographic key that is required by the *munge* authentication
library to be available on every host in the resource management pool. The
CURVE certificate holds the system instance's secret key, so it goes with the
munge key in the `secrets` runtime overlay, which warewulfd serves only to root
on the nodes. A systemd drop-in has munge and the Flux broker start after
`wwclient` has applied it. To import these, issue the following:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
```bash
# Configure the Flux system instance and the IMP
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig /etc/flux/system/conf.d/system.toml
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig /etc/flux/imp/conf.d/imp.toml

# The CURVE certificate in the runtime overlay, readable by flux only
wwctl overlay import --parents secrets /etc/flux/system/curve.cert
wwctl overlay chown secrets /etc/flux/system/curve.cert \
	"$(id -u flux):$(id -g flux)"
wwctl overlay chmod secrets /etc/flux/system/curve.cert 0400

# Configure munge: the key in the runtime overlay, readable by munge only
wwctl overlay import --parents secrets /etc/munge/munge.key
wwctl overlay chown secrets /etc/munge/munge.key "$(id -u munge):$(id -g munge)"
wwctl overlay chown secrets /etc/munge "$(id -u munge):$(id -g munge)"
wwctl overlay chmod secrets /etc/munge 0700
wwctl overlay chmod secrets /etc/munge/munge.key 0400

# Start munge and flux after wwclient has applied the runtime overlay
# (munge key, CURVE certificate)
for unit in munge.service flux.service; do
	wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig \
		/opt/ohpc/admin/warewulf/wait-wwclient.conf \
		/etc/systemd/system/${unit}.d/wait-wwclient.conf
done
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
